course: dictionary
lesson: 6646
title: Bright sea slugs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nudibranch is a kind of sea animal. The words around it give you clues: «Sea slugs called nudibranchs are bright to warn that they taste bad or sting.» The word called shows that nudibranch is a name, and sea slug tells you it lives in the sea.
explain: Bright is another clue. The sentence says the colours are a warning, so the bright colours send a message to other animals. Ask yourself what would fit: a sea animal whose bright colours tell hungry animals to keep away.
explain: Many nudibranchs have no shell, so their colours help keep them safe. Some even keep tiny algae inside them and make food from sunlight, as the example sentence shows. Context helps you learn what a word means and why it matters.
fact: A nudibranch is a sea slug, often brightly coloured, with no shell.
fact: Nudibranchs live in the sea, often on reefs and rocks.
fact: Their bright colours warn predators that they taste bad or are poisonous.
fact: Some nudibranchs store the stings of the animals they eat.
fact: Context clues, such as «called» and «warn», can help you work out what a new word means.
exercise: What is a nudibranch? | *A kind of sea slug | A sea bird that dives for food | A type of seaweed | A fish with fins
exercise: «The bright colours warn predators.» What do the bright colours tell other animals? | *Keep away, this animal may taste bad or sting | It is ready to sleep | Come and play | It is very cold
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Sea slugs called nudibranchs are bright to warn» that tells you a nudibranch is a type of sea slug. | *called | bright | warn | sea
test: Which animal is a nudibranch? | A bird that flies over the waves | A crab with two large claws | A snail with a big shell on its back | *A sea slug with bright colours and no shell
test: In «bright to warn that they taste bad», what does warn mean? | To tickle someone | To hide from danger | To wake someone up | *To tell others to keep away
exam: Which word in «Sea slugs called nudibranchs are bright to warn that they taste bad or sting» tells you the colours are a message? | *warn | slugs | nudibranchs | sea
